Problem:    I would like to have getty autobaud to 19200, the getty
	    in ULTRIX 3.0 (VAX) doesn't seem to support this speed.
	    Am I correct, and if so, is there a way to patch getty
	    to support a speed of 19200?

Hardare:    MVAX II, DHV11 serial multiplexer
OS:	    ULTRIX 3.0
Program:    /usr/etc/getty
Modem:      FastComm 9696 (capable of 19200 baud)


In /etc/ttys, the following line is defined:

ttyd0   "/etc/getty sec19200" dialup on  modem shared	# fastcomm  in/out


In /etc/gettytab, the following entries are defined:

sec19200:\
	:im=\r\n\r\n\[text deleted]:\
	:lo=/bin/login:nx=sec9600:tc=std.19200:

sec9600:\
	:im=\r\n\r\n\[text deleted]:\
	:lo=/bin/login:nx=sec2400:tc=std.9600:

sec2400:\
	:im=\r\n\r\n\[text deleted]:\
	:lo=/bin/login:nx=sec1200:tc=std.2400:

sec1200:\
	:im=\r\n\r\n\[text deleted]:\
	:lo=/bin/login:nx=sec19200:tc=std.1200:


Everything works great for speeds of 9600, 2400, 1200.  The problem
seems to be that getty doesn't know how to autobaud to 19200, and then
falls to 9600.  

While 9600 baud is great, it seems that 19200 should be supportable.
FastComm modems are being used at each end, so communications at 19200
are possible.  If I hardwire the answering modem to talk to the local
DTE at 19200, things work well.  However, since I need to support
connections at lower speeds and the buffering capabilities of slower
modems is not perfect, I have set the modems up so that they force the
DTE speed to be equal to that of the incoming call.

My hope is that there is a patch available for getty that will allow
me to replace an unused speed entry (300 baud) with an entry for
19200. 

Thanks everyone.

-- 
